title: Daraxonrasib - second-line and later metastatic pancreatic cancer
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

* ''Role:'' Daraxonrasib (RMC-6236), an oral RAS(ON) multiselective inhibitor, improves second-line survival in metastatic pancreatic ductal adenocarcinoma. FDA-approved August 26, 2026 after ≥1 prior systemic therapy, without a RAS-mutation requirement.
* ''RASolute 302 (phase 3):'' 500 patients progressing after one systemic line; ECOG performance status 0–1; 91.8% RAS G12-mutant. Randomized daraxonrasib versus investigator-choice chemotherapy. Overall-population median overall survival (OS) ''13.2 vs 6.7 months'' (hazard ratio 0.40); progression-free survival (PFS) ''7.2 vs 3.6 months'' (hazard ratio 0.49); objective response ''30% vs 11%''. Benefit in the overall population does not establish equal efficacy across uncommon RAS subgroups.
* ''Third line and beyond:'' Phase 1/2 cohort, 46 RAS-mutant patients with 2–5 prior metastatic regimens; median follow-up 22.6 months. Objective response ''20%'' (95% CI 9–34), disease control 85%, median PFS ''4.3 months'', OS ''9.0 months''. Single-arm ASCO 2026 abstract: activity signal, without randomized proof of superiority in this setting.
* ''Toxicity:'' Rash, diarrhea, and stomatitis/mucositis are prominent. Phase 3 grade ≥3 treatment-emergent adverse events: 61.8% versus 69.6%; treatment-related discontinuation: 1.2% versus 11.2%.
* ''Recall:'' Second-line randomized benefit is the strongest evidence; later-line use has weaker direct evidence.

Sources: [[O'Reilly 2026|https://doi.org/10.1056/NEJMoa2605555]]; [[Garrido-Laguna ASCO 2026, e15104|https://doi.org/10.1200/JCO.2026.44.16_suppl.e15104]]; [[FDA 2026|https://www.fda.gov/drugs/resources-information-approved-drugs/fda-approves-daraxonrasib-metastatic-pancreatic-adenocarcinoma]]; ASCO SEP 2026, ch. 13.1, pp. 658–659.
